export default [{"id":"rb01","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 1","topics":"Home, friends and hobbies · Reading a book and watching television · A family tradition · Having a hobby","part1_1":["What do you enjoy most about your home?","Describe your best friend.","What is your favourite hobby?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of reading a book in your free time?","Why do most people prefer watching television in the evening?"],"part2":["Describe a tradition that is important in your family or in your region.","How is this tradition usually celebrated?","Why is it important for young people to keep old traditions alive?"],"part3":{"statement":"Everyone should have a hobby.","for":["a healthy way to relieve stress after work or study","builds new skills and often new friendships","encourages creativity and personal growth"],"against":["not everyone has the free time or the money for one","some hobbies are expensive or even risky","a hobby can become an obsession and take over normal life"]},"part1_2_images":["rb01_p12_1.jpg","rb01_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb01_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb02","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 2","topics":"Music, books and evenings · Paper books and electronic books · Time passing quickly or slowly · Standardised testing","part1_1":["What kind of music do you enjoy listening to?","Do you have many books at home?","What do you usually do to relax at home?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of reading a printed book?","Why have electronic books become so popular in recent years?"],"part2":["Describe a time when the hours passed very quickly, or very slowly.","What were you doing and how did you feel?","How important is good time management for a person's success?"],"part3":{"statement":"Standardised tests should be removed from schools.","for":["one exam cannot measure a student's real ability","teachers end up teaching only what will be tested","creates serious stress and anxiety among young people"],"against":["gives a fair and equal measure for every student","universities and employers need a comparable result","shows which schools and regions need more support"]},"part1_2_images":["rb02_p12_1.jpg","rb02_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb02_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb03","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 3","topics":"Room, music and television · Phone photographs and camera photographs · Something that did not meet your expectations ·","part1_1":["How is your room decorated?","What is your favourite song?","Do you watch much television?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","Why do so many people prefer taking photographs with a phone?","What can a professional camera do that a phone cannot?"],"part2":["Describe a time when something did not meet your expectations.","What had you expected, and what actually happened?","Is it better to have high expectations or low ones?"],"part3":{"statement":"Professional athletes are paid far too much money.","for":["their salaries are out of proportion to teachers and doctors","the money could fund grassroots sport for ordinary children","huge pay gives young fans the wrong idea about success"],"against":["their careers are short and can end with one injury","they generate enormous income through tickets and sponsors","very few people in the world reach that level of talent"]},"part1_2_images":["rb03_p12_1.jpg","rb03_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb03_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb04","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 4","topics":"Neighbourhood, friends and the internet · Travelling by bus and by bicycle · Working as part of a team · Tourism in historical","part1_1":["Tell me about your neighbourhood.","How do you usually travel around your city?","Do you prefer spending time alone or with other people?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the benefits of cycling to work or to school?","Why do most people in your country use public transport instead?"],"part2":["Describe a time when you worked as part of a team.","What was your own role in that team?","What are the benefits of working together to reach a goal?"],"part3":{"statement":"The number of tourists allowed into historical cities should be limited.","for":["protects fragile monuments from damage and overcrowding","improves daily life for the people who live there","a calmer visit is a better experience for the tourist too"],"against":["tourism is a major source of income and local jobs","everyone has the right to see their own cultural heritage","the money from visitors pays for restoration work"]},"part1_2_images":["rb04_p12_1.jpg","rb04_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb04_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb05","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 5","topics":"Family, breakfast and travel · Living in a flat and living in a house · Doing something on your own · Space tourism","part1_1":["Describe your family.","Tell me about the nicest place you have ever visited.","What do you usually do with your family at the weekend?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of living in a house with a garden?","Why do so many people choose to live in a flat in the city?"],"part2":["Describe a time when you did something important completely on your own.","How did you feel while you were doing it?","At what age should young people start becoming independent?"],"part3":{"statement":"Space tourism should be banned.","for":["every flight releases an enormous amount of pollution","the money would do more good solving problems on Earth","it is a luxury only the very richest people can buy"],"against":["private spending speeds up space technology for everyone","it creates highly skilled jobs and whole new industries","exploration has always pushed human knowledge forward"]},"part1_2_images":["rb05_p12_1.jpg","rb05_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb05_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb06","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 6","topics":"Home, pets and food · Talking on the phone and talking face to face · Advice you were given · Video games","part1_1":["Describe your home.","Do you have any pets?","What is your favourite meal of the day?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of talking to someone face to face?","Why do people often prefer to call or message instead?"],"part2":["Describe a time when someone gave you useful advice.","Who gave you that advice, and did you follow it?","Why do some people find it difficult to accept advice?"],"part3":{"statement":"Video games are beneficial for young people.","for":["improve reaction speed, memory and problem-solving","many games are played in teams and build cooperation","a cheap and social way for young people to relax"],"against":["long hours of screen time harm health and sleep","take time away from study, sport and real friendships","some games are violent or designed to be addictive"]},"part1_2_images":["rb06_p12_1.jpg","rb06_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb06_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb07","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 7","topics":"Neighbourhood, friends and evenings · Studying alone and studying in a group · Setting yourself a goal · Teaching handwriting","part1_1":["Can you describe the area where you live?","Who is your closest friend and why?","How do you usually spend your evenings?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of studying on your own?","Why do many students learn better in a group?"],"part2":["Describe an ambitious goal that you set for yourself.","How did it affect your personal and your professional life?","Are there any drawbacks to being a very ambitious person?"],"part3":{"statement":"Handwriting should still be taught in schools.","for":["writing by hand helps children remember what they learn","develops fine motor control and concentration","pen and paper always work, with no battery or signal"],"against":["almost all adult work is now done on a keyboard","those hours could be spent on digital skills instead","typing is faster and far easier for everyone to read"]},"part1_2_images":["rb07_p12_1.jpg","rb07_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb07_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb08","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 8","topics":"Room, health and routine · How older and younger people spend time · Forgiving someone · Keeping pets","part1_1":["Tell me about your room.","What do you do to stay healthy?","Do you usually get up early or late?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","How do older and younger people spend their free time differently?","What can younger people learn from spending time with older people?"],"part2":["Describe a time when you forgave someone, or someone forgave you.","What had happened between you?","Why is forgiveness important in a family or a friendship?"],"part3":{"statement":"Keeping a pet improves a person's quality of life.","for":["offers companionship and real emotional support","teaches responsibility, routine and patience","owners walk more and are generally more active"],"against":["pets cost money and need daily time and attention","unsuitable for small flats or very busy households","losing a pet causes genuine and lasting distress"]},"part1_2_images":["rb08_p12_1.jpg","rb08_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb08_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb09","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 9","topics":"Family time, home and food · Free time alone and with other people · A regret you have · Animals in zoos","part1_1":["Do you usually spend much time with your family?","Describe your bedroom.","What is your favourite dish?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of spending free time on your own?","Why do most people prefer to relax with friends or family?"],"part2":["Describe something in your life that you regret.","What would you do differently if you could go back?","Can regret ever have a positive effect on a person?"],"part3":{"statement":"Animals should be kept in their natural habitat, not in zoos.","for":["animals live freely and behave naturally in the wild","captivity causes stress and unnatural behaviour","it respects animal rights and prevents mistreatment"],"against":["zoos protect and breed endangered species","they teach the public to care about wildlife","scientists can study animals closely and safely"]},"part1_2_images":["rb09_p12_1.jpg","rb09_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb09_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"rb10","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set B · Test 10","topics":"School, routine and weather · Traditional and modern classrooms · Feeling confident in yourself · Online privacy","part1_1":["Describe your school or your workplace.","What time do you usually wake up?","What is the weather like today?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of a modern, flexible classroom?","Why do many teachers still prefer a traditional classroom?"],"part2":["Describe a time when you felt truly confident in yourself.","What had given you that confidence?","How can a person build real self-confidence?"],"part3":{"statement":"Online privacy is more important than national security.","for":["privacy is a basic right of every citizen","collected data can be leaked, stolen or misused","mass surveillance rarely stops serious crime"],"against":["monitoring helps prevent terrorism and organised crime","online data protects children from exploitation","honest people lose very little by being checked"]},"part1_2_images":["rb10_p12_1.jpg","rb10_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"rb10_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra01","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 1","topics":"Home and evenings · Healthy food and fast food · Sharing a secret · Calorie information in restaurants","part1_1":["Do you live in a house or in a flat?","What do you usually do in the evening?","Do you like cooking?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What is the biggest difficulty people face in keeping to a healthy diet?","How can we encourage more people to eat healthy food?"],"part2":["Describe a time when you shared a secret with someone.","Why did you decide to share it with that person?","How important is trust between people?"],"part3":{"statement":"Fast-food restaurants should display the number of calories in their meals.","for":["helps people make an informed choice about what they eat","encourages restaurants to offer healthier options","could reduce obesity and diet-related illness"],"against":["most customers ignore the numbers anyway","can create anxiety and guilt around food","calories say nothing about the real nutritional value"]},"part1_2_images":["ra01_p12_1.jpg","ra01_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra01_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra02","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 2","topics":"Sport and your town · Paying in cash and by card · A time you felt powerful · A four-day working week","part1_1":["Tell me about a sport that you play or watch.","What do you like most about your town?","Who is your favourite sportsperson?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","Why do some people prefer paying by card?","What are the advantages of paying in cash?"],"part2":["Describe a time when you felt powerful.","What exactly gave you that feeling?","Do you think having power changes the way people behave?"],"part3":{"statement":"Employees should work only four days a week.","for":["rested workers are more productive in fewer hours","more time for family, study and personal health","fewer working days mean less commuting and pollution"],"against":["many services must operate five or six days a week","the same workload is squeezed into longer days","small businesses may lose income and customers"]},"part1_2_images":["ra02_p12_1.jpg","ra02_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra02_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra03","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 3","topics":"Hobbies and music · Watching television and playing board games · A person close to you · Children and mobile phones","part1_1":["What is your hobby?","Which part of the day do you like the most?","What kind of music do you like?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of playing board games together?","Why do many families prefer watching television in the evening?"],"part2":["Describe a person who is very close to you.","How did you first meet this person?","Why is that person so important in your life?"],"part3":{"statement":"Children should spend far less time on mobile phones.","for":["protects eyesight, sleep and physical activity","more real conversation with family and friends","less exposure to harmful or unsuitable content"],"against":["phones are now a normal learning and study tool","parents need a way to stay in contact with children","the problem is how phones are used, not the time itself"]},"part1_2_images":["ra03_p12_1.jpg","ra03_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra03_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra04","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 4","topics":"Family, books and films · Writing by hand and typing · An uncertain situation · Homework","part1_1":["Do you have a large family?","How often do you read books?","Do you have a favourite actor or actress?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of writing by hand?","Why do most students now prefer typing on a computer?"],"part2":["Describe a situation when you did not know what to do.","How did you finally make your decision?","How do people usually behave when their future is uncertain?"],"part3":{"statement":"Homework should be abolished in schools.","for":["children need rest, sport and family time after lessons","homework increases stress and copying instead of learning","not every family can help with difficult tasks at home"],"against":["practice at home fixes what was taught in class","teaches independence, planning and self-discipline","prepares students for university and for exams"]},"part1_2_images":["ra04_p12_1.jpg","ra04_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra04_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra05","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 5","topics":"Work, study and free time · Local markets and supermarkets · An important decision · Free university education","part1_1":["Do you work or do you study?","Where do you like to go in your free time?","Do you have a lot of friends?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of shopping at a local market?","Why do so many people prefer supermarkets these days?"],"part2":["Tell me about an important decision that you have made.","How has this decision influenced your life?","What has the greatest effect on the decisions that people make?"],"part3":{"statement":"University education should be free for everyone.","for":["talented students are not stopped by their family income","a better educated population helps the whole economy","reduces inequality between rich and poor regions"],"against":["a very heavy cost for the state budget and taxpayers","free places may be taken by unmotivated students","quality can fall when universities are underfunded"]},"part1_2_images":["ra05_p12_1.jpg","ra05_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra05_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra06","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 6","topics":"Weekends and weather · Driving a car and using public transport · Achieving success · Electric cars","part1_1":["What kind of weather do you dislike?","Who do you usually spend your weekends with?","How often do you use your phone?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of using public transport?","Why do many people still prefer to drive their own car?"],"part2":["Describe something you did in your life that was a success.","How did this success affect you and the people around you?","What role do hard work, talent and opportunity play in success?"],"part3":{"statement":"Electric cars should completely replace petrol cars.","for":["much cleaner air in crowded cities","cheaper to run and to maintain over time","reduces a country's dependence on imported fuel"],"against":["very few charging stations outside big cities","the purchase price is still too high for most families","producing and recycling batteries also harms the environment"]},"part1_2_images":["ra06_p12_1.jpg","ra06_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra06_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra07","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 7","topics":"Daily habits and music · Camping and staying in a hotel · Disagreeing with someone · Taxes on fast food","part1_1":["Do you get up early or late?","What kind of clothes do you usually wear?","Do you listen to music every day?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of going camping?","Why do some people prefer staying in a hotel?"],"part2":["Tell me about a time when you disagreed with someone.","What was the situation and how did you express your disagreement?","What is the best way to disagree with a person politely?"],"part3":{"statement":"Fast food should be taxed much more heavily.","for":["higher prices push people towards healthier choices","the money raised can fund healthcare and sport","encourages companies to improve what they sell"],"against":["hits low-income families hardest of all","adults should be free to choose their own diet","may damage small businesses and cost jobs"]},"part1_2_images":["ra07_p12_1.jpg","ra07_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra07_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra08","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 8","topics":"Routine, food and health · Life in a city and in the countryside · Feeling truly free · Art classes at school","part1_1":["What do you do after work or after school?","What is your favourite meal of the day?","What do you do to stay healthy?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","Which place would you prefer to live in, and why?","What are the advantages of living in each of these places?"],"part2":["Tell me about a moment when you felt truly free.","Where were you and what were you doing?","What stops people from feeling free in everyday life?"],"part3":{"statement":"Art classes should be compulsory in every school.","for":["develops creativity and problem-solving","gives students a way to express feelings","improves results in other academic subjects too"],"against":["takes lesson time from maths, science and languages","schools lack materials and trained art teachers","students with no interest gain very little from it"]},"part1_2_images":["ra08_p12_1.jpg","ra08_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra08_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra09","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 9","topics":"Cooking, cinema and museums · Shopping online and in a store · A festival you enjoyed · Limits on personal income","part1_1":["What do you usually cook at home?","How often do you go to the cinema?","Are museums popular in your country?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of shopping online?","Why do many people still prefer to shop in a real store?"],"part2":["Describe a festival that you really enjoyed.","Who did you celebrate it with?","Why are traditional festivals important for a country?"],"part3":{"statement":"Governments should limit how much money one person can earn.","for":["reduces the gap between the richest and the poorest","more money left for wages and public services","limits the political power of very wealthy individuals"],"against":["removes the motivation to build and to invest","talented people will simply move to other countries","success should be rewarded, not punished"]},"part1_2_images":["ra09_p12_1.jpg","ra09_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra09_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"ra10","title":"Real Exam 2026 · Set A · Test 10","topics":"Animals, music and outdoor life · At the cinema and watching films at home · Noticing inequality · Performance pay in sport","part1_1":["Do you like animals?","Who is your favourite singer?","What outdoor activities do you do?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of watching a film at the cinema?","Why do many people prefer watching films at home?"],"part2":["Describe a time when you noticed or experienced inequality.","What did that experience teach you?","What effect does inequality have on a society?"],"part3":{"statement":"Sports teams should be allowed to pay players according to their performance.","for":["rewards hard work, skill and real results","motivates every player to give their best","makes teams more competitive and financially efficient"],"against":["creates unhealthy competition inside the team","players in defensive roles get fewer chances to shine","focuses attention on individuals rather than teamwork"]},"part1_2_images":["ra10_p12_1.jpg","ra10_p12_2.jpg"],"part2_image":"ra10_p2.jpg","source":"Real Exam Questions (MultiLevelRecord)"},{"id":"mb03","title":"Mock Book · Mock 3","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Where do you like to go to in your free time?","Do you work or study?","Do you like listening to music?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","Why do some people like to eat fast food?","Do you think breakfast is important?"],"part1_2_images":["mb03_p12_1.jpg","mb03_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Tell me about a skill you have learned recently.","Why is it important nowadays?","Give an example of when you use this skill."],"part2_image":"mb03_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"The arts should be supported by the government.","for":["People can learn from art","Art encourages creativity and promotes harmony in society","The government is responsible for protecting the culture"],"against":["Funding could be better granted to education and the healthcare system","Art does not play a vital role in society","Artists should earn their own living"]},"model":{"part1_1":["I enjoy spending my free time in a variety of ways, but I'm particularly drawn to places that offer a sense of tranquility and rejuvenation. For example, I often visit the local park, where I can take a leisurely stroll, enjoy the fresh air, and observe nature. I also find museums to be incredibly stimulating environments, as they expose me to new ideas and perspectives. And of course, I always appreciate spending time with friends and family, whether it's catching a movie or simply having a meal together.","Right now, I'm focusing on my studies, which is keeping me quite busy. I'm currently pursuing a degree in English Literature, and I'm really enjoying the challenges and opportunities that come with it. The academic environment is very stimulating, and I'm constantly learning and expanding my knowledge.","Absolutely! Music is an integral part of my life, and I enjoy listening to a wide range of genres. I'm particularly fond of pop and soul music for their energy, emotional depth, complexity. Music has the power to uplift my mood, provide comfort, and inspire creativity. I find myself listening to music almost every day, whether it's while I'm studying, working out, or simply relaxing at home."],"part1_2":["The first picture shows a mother and her young daughter enjoying a meal together in a restaurant, probably a fast-food place. They're both smiling and seem relaxed, and the mother's got a classic burger and fries, while her daughter has her own meal. There's a glass of juice for refreshment, which adds to the casual, fun atmosphere that you often get when dining out. The second picture, on the other hand, shows a woman preparing a meal in her kitchen. She's carefully arranging fresh vegetables on her kitchen table, likely to chop them up for a dish. This picture really highlights the methodical and purposeful nature of home cooking.","There are several reasons why people are drawn to fast food. Convenience is a major factor. Fast food restaurants are readily available and offer quick service, appealing to busy individuals with limited time. The affordability of fast food also makes it an attractive option, particularly for those on a budget. Additionally, the familiar flavors and textures of fast food can be comforting and satisfying, offering a quick escape from the everyday. However, it's important to note that fast food is often high in calories, fat, and sodium, and consuming it regularly can have negative health implications.","I firmly believe that breakfast is an essential meal of the day. It provides the body with vital nutrients and energy after a long night of rest. This can improve concentration, focus, and overall energy levels throughout the day. Studies have shown that people who eat breakfast tend to have healthier eating habits overall and may even be less likely to be overweight or obese. While I understand that some people don't have time for a full breakfast, even a simple snack like a piece of fruit or a yogurt can be a helpful way to start the day."],"part2":"Recently, I've been really dedicated to improving my English language skills. I've always been interested in different cultures and languages, and English is the global language of communication. I've been taking online courses that focus on both grammar and vocabulary, and I've been making a conscious effort to practice speaking with native speakers. It's been a challenging yet rewarding journey, and I'm really pleased with how much my fluency and confidence have improved. I'm now able to express myself more clearly and effectively, which is crucial for my personal and professional growth.\" \"In today's globalized world, English proficiency is essential for countless aspects of life. It opens doors to a wider range of opportunities in education, employment, and travel. It allows individuals to connect with people from diverse cultures, access information from around the world, and thrive in an increasingly interconnected society. It's not just about being able to communicate, it's about being able to understand and engage with different perspectives and ideas.\" \"Just the other day, I was participating in an online discussion forum about current events. It was fascinating to see how people from all over the world shared their viewpoints and engaged in respectful debate. I was able to contribute my own thoughts and perspectives, and I learned a lot from the different perspectives shared. This experience really highlighted the importance of effective communication and how English can be a bridge to understanding different cultures and perspectives.","part3":"The argument for government support of the arts rests on the undeniable value it brings to society. Beyond mere entertainment, art serves as a powerful educational tool, fostering critical thinking and diverse perspectives. A visit to a museum can transport viewers to distant times and cultures, broadening their horizons and enriching their understanding of the world. Additionally, art promotes creativity and innovation, vital qualities for individual and societal progress. Whether through painting, music, or theatre, art encourages expression and imagination, sparking new ideas and fostering a vibrant and dynamic cultural landscape. Moreover, governments have a responsibility to protect and preserve cultural heritage, and art plays a central role in this endeavor. By supporting artistic endeavors, governments ensure the continuation of a rich tapestry of traditions, stories, and expressions that define a nation's identity. While the merits of art are undeniable, opponents argue that government funding should be prioritized for essential services like education and healthcare. They maintain that art, while enriching, is a luxury that individuals can support through private patronage. In their view, art does not play a vital role in society, and artists should be able to earn a living through their craft, just like any other profession. They argue that government resources are better allocated to areas that directly impact the well-being and economic prosperity of citizens, leaving art to thrive or fail based on its inherent value and the support it receives from individuals and private organizations."}},{"id":"mb04","title":"Mock Book · Mock 4","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Do you live in a flat or a house?","What is your favorite animal?","Do you like sport?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of online learning?","What are the advantages of traditional studying?"],"part1_2_images":["mb04_p12_1.jpg","mb04_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Tell me about a critical decision you have made.","How has this decision influenced you and your life?","What factors have the highest impact on the decisions people make?"],"part2_image":"mb04_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Single-use plastic should be banned.","for":["Cleaner environment","Saves animals","Less waste"],"against":["Single-use things are cheaper","It can be hard to find reusable options for everything","Some people might lose their jobs in companies"]},"model":{"part1_1":["I live in a flat, actually. It's quite cozy and practical for me. I enjoy having easy access to amenities and the convenience of living in a central location. While I appreciate the spaciousness of a house, I think a flat suits my lifestyle better, especially since I enjoy spending time exploring the city and connecting with friends.","I'm a big fan of dolphins! They're so intelligent and playful. I love watching documentaries about them and learning about how they communicate and work together. They're also fascinating creatures because they're so adaptable and can thrive in different environments. I think their playful nature and strong social bonds are quite inspiring.","I'm a big sports fan! I love watching football and basketball. I find it really exciting to see athletes pushing their limits and working together as a team. I also enjoy the strategic side of the game and how it involves both physical skill and mental strategy. It's a great way to unwind and get swept up in the action."],"part1_2":["These pictures illustrate two contrasting approaches to learning: traditional classroom instruction and the increasingly popular online learning environment. The first picture evokes a sense of warmth and community, with students engaged in a traditional classroom setting. The children's focused expressions and sparkling eyes suggest active participation and a genuine interest in their teacher's instruction. It highlights the importance of face-to-face interaction and the role of a teacher as a guide and facilitator of learning. The second picture, however, depicts a more solitary experience, with a student focused intently on an online learning platform. The use of headphones emphasizes the individual nature of online learning and the reliance on technology. While it offers flexibility and access to a vast array of resources, it raises questions about the potential for isolation and the importance of fostering a sense of community among online learners.","Online learning has become incredibly popular, and for good reason. One of the biggest advantages is its flexibility. You can study at your own pace, from anywhere in the world, which is great for busy people or those with family commitments. Additionally, online platforms offer a wealth of resources and information that might not be readily available in traditional settings. You can also find specialized courses and connect with a global community of learners.","Traditional learning in a classroom setting still holds its own. It provides a structured learning environment, with clear deadlines and direct interaction with professors. This structure can be beneficial for some learners who prefer a more disciplined approach. Additionally, traditional classrooms offer the opportunity for face-to-face interaction with peers, fostering collaboration and a sense of community. The social aspect can be very valuable for many students."],"part2":"One of the most critical decisions I made was choosing to pursue a master's degree abroad. At the time, I was weighing the pros and cons of continuing my education in my home country versus venturing into an international environment. Ultimately, I decided that studying abroad would not only enhance my academic credentials but also broaden my cultural horizons and professional network. This choice was pivotal, as it exposed me to diverse perspectives and methodologies, significantly enriching my understanding of my field. This decision has profoundly influenced both my personal and professional development. Academically, I acquired advanced knowledge and skills that have set me apart in the job market. On a personal level, living in a foreign country challenged me to adapt to new cultures and navigate various social dynamics, fostering resilience and independence. Additionally, the friendships I formed with individuals from different backgrounds have enriched my life immeasurably, providing me with a global perspective that informs my worldview. Overall, this experience has instilled in me a lifelong passion for learning and exploration. Several factors significantly impact the decisions people make, with personal values and life experiences often being paramount. Individuals tend to base their choices on what aligns with their core beliefs and priorities. Additionally, social influences, such as family expectations and peer pressure, can heavily sway decisions, particularly in formative years. Economic considerations also play a crucial role; for instance, financial stability can dictate career choices or educational pursuits. Finally, emotional factors—such as fear of failure or desire for security—often complicate decision-making processes, leading individuals to weigh risks against potential rewards carefully.","part3":"A ban on single-use plastic would bring about significant environmental benefits. Firstly, it would dramatically reduce plastic waste, mitigating the detrimental impact of plastic pollution on our oceans, beaches, and wildlife. The presence of plastic debris in our ecosystems not only disrupts the natural balance but also poses a threat to marine life through ingestion and entanglement. Secondly, a ban would encourage the adoption of sustainable alternatives, such as reusable bags, containers, and biodegradable packaging. This shift towards eco-friendly options would minimize our reliance on fossil fuels and reduce the carbon footprint associated with plastic production. Finally, banning single-use plastic would promote a circular economy, where resources are used more efficiently, minimizing waste and promoting resource conservation. This shift towards a more sustainable model of consumption is essential for safeguarding our planet for future generations. Despite the potential benefits, banning single-use plastic also presents some challenges. Firstly, it could lead to economic disruption for industries reliant on plastic production and packaging. This could result in job losses and price increases for consumers as companies transition to more sustainable alternatives. Secondly, a ban could pose challenges for affordability and accessibility, particularly for low-income communities. Reusable alternatives can often be more expensive than single-use options, potentially exacerbating existing inequalities. Finally, implementing a comprehensive ban would require significant infrastructure development, consumer education, and robust enforcement mechanisms. Ensuring effective implementation across different sectors and communities would be a complex task, requiring substantial investment and coordination."}},{"id":"mb05","title":"Mock Book · Mock 5","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["When do you usually listen to music?","What do you do to stay healthy?","Tell me about your school."],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What is the advantage of buying products from local farmers over the supermarket?","What is the advantage of buying products from a supermarket?"],"part1_2_images":["mb05_p12_1.jpg","mb05_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a special meal that someone prepared for you.","Who cooked it for you?","How did you feel about it?"],"part2_image":"mb05_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Students should wear uniforms at school.","for":["School uniforms promote a sense of equality among students","Students are less likely to be preoccupied with their appearance or compare themselves to others","Uniforms create a strong sense of unity"],"against":["School uniforms can be expensive","Uniforms may not always be comfortable","The same clothes limit pupils' ability to express themselves through their clothing choices"]},"model":{"part1_1":["I find myself listening to music most often when I'm winding down after a busy day. It helps me to relax and de-stress, especially after work or studying. I also enjoy listening to music while I'm exercising, as it provides a great motivational boost and helps me to stay focused.","Maintaining a healthy lifestyle is important to me. I try to eat a balanced diet, focusing on fresh fruits, vegetables, and whole grains. I also prioritize regular exercise, aiming for at least 30 minutes of physical activity most days of the week. I find that a combination of cardio and strength training helps to keep me fit and energized.","I attended a large, public high school with a diverse student population. It was known for its strong academic programs and extracurricular activities. The teachers were dedicated and supportive, creating a positive learning environment. While the school was quite large, I was fortunate to find a close group of friends who shared similar interests."],"part1_2":["Both images represent distinct shopping experiences. The first image highlights the convenience of supermarkets, where families can shop together in a comfortable environment. Supermarkets often offer a wide range of products under one roof, making it easier for families to find everything they need in one trip. In contrast, the second image features a street market; bustling with activity and showcasing a variety of fresh fruits and people are engaging with one another while exploring different stalls.","Buying directly from local farmers offers several advantages over supermarket shopping. Firstly, it promotes sustainability by supporting local businesses and reducing the environmental impact of long- distance transportation. Secondly, you often get fresher, higher-quality produce, as it hasn't traveled long distances and is picked at peak ripeness. Additionally, interacting with the farmers themselves allows you to learn about their practices and ask questions about their products, building a stronger connection to your food source.","Supermarkets provide a convenient and readily accessible option for purchasing a wide range of goods. They offer a vast selection of products from various brands and regions, catering to diverse dietary needs and preferences. Additionally, supermarkets are often conveniently located, with extended opening hours and a variety of payment methods. This convenience, coupled with the wide selection, makes them a popular choice for many shoppers."],"part2":"One special meal that stands out in my memory was prepared by my mother on my birthday last year. She decided to cook my favorite dish: a classic homemade chicken curry, accompanied by fragrant rice and fresh bread. My mother has always been an incredible cook, and her chicken curry is something I’ve cherished since childhood. The moment I walked into the kitchen, the aroma of spices filled the air, instantly making my mouth water. She spent hours preparing the meal, carefully selecting the freshest ingredients and blending them to perfection. When we finally sat down to eat, I felt a wave of warmth and happiness. It wasn’t just about the delicious food; it was also about the love and effort she put into making my birthday special. Sharing that meal with my family made it even more meaningful. We laughed, reminisced, and enjoyed each other’s company, creating memories that I will hold dear. Overall, this meal was more than just sustenance; it was a heartfelt expression of love from my mother. It reminded me of the importance of family traditions and the joy that comes from sharing good food with loved ones.","part3":"On one hand, school uniforms offer a number of benefits. They promote a sense of equality among students, regardless of their background or socioeconomic status. When everyone is dressed alike, there's less pressure to conform to expensive trends or feel inferior because of their clothing. This can create a more focused learning environment, as students are less likely to be preoccupied with their appearance or comparing themselves to others. Uniforms also foster a sense of unity and belonging within the school community, creating a shared identity that reinforces school values and traditions. However, the argument against school uniforms highlights a few drawbacks. Firstly, uniforms can be expensive, especially for families with multiple children. This can be a financial burden, particularly for those who are already struggling to make ends meet. Secondly, uniforms may not always be comfortable or practical for all students, especially during different weather conditions or if they participate in physically demanding activities. Perhaps the most significant argument against uniforms is that they limit students' ability to express themselves through their clothing choices. For many, fashion is a form of personal expression, and being forced to wear the same clothes every day can stifle their creativity and individuality."}},{"id":"mb06","title":"Mock Book · Mock 6","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Describe your house.","Do you get up early or late?","What is your favourite drink?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the benefits of travelling by train?","Which ways of travelling do you prefer?"],"part1_2_images":["mb06_p12_1.jpg","mb06_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a time when you achieved a great goal.","Describe a person who influenced you.","How did you feel about this achievement?"],"part2_image":"mb06_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Smartphones should be banned in schools.","for":["Better focus and learning","More time for real-life activities","Reduced screen time and eye strain"],"against":["Limited access to information","Restricted communication","Limited use for educational purposes"]},"model":{"part1_1":["My house is a comfortable two-story terraced house in a quiet neighborhood. It's quite spacious with a cozy living room, a well-equipped kitchen, and a small but sunny garden. I really enjoy spending time in my garden, especially during the warmer months.","I tend to be a bit of a morning person, so I usually wake up quite early, around 7:00 am. It gives me a chance to start my day calmly and have a good breakfast before starting work or my studies.","Actually, my preference in terms of beverages quite diversifies. It depends on what I am having or what I am doing. When I am having lunch, I prefer to drink hot tea rather than fizzy drinks. In contrast, when I am engaged in physical activities, I would like to have mineral water. Or, on chilly days, drinking hot coffee is my cup of tea."],"part1_2":["These two images offer a fascinating contrast between two popular modes of travel. In the first, we see passengers boarding an airplane, a method that prioritizes speed and efficiency. While air travel can be expensive, it undeniably saves a considerable amount of time, making it ideal for long-distance journeys or those with tight schedules. In the second image, however, we observe a scenic train journey, where travelers can immerse themselves in breathtaking views. This leisurely pace allows for a more relaxed and enjoyable experience, allowing passengers to truly appreciate the landscapes they pass through. Ultimately, the choice between air and rail travel comes down to personal priorities: time versus tranquility, cost versus scenery.","Trains offer a number of advantages. Firstly, they are often more affordable than other modes of transport, making them accessible to a wider range of travelers. You can also comfortably use your electronic devices, work, or relax during the journey. And unlike planes, train travel is generally not affected by weather conditions, so you can be confident you'll reach your destination. Plus, many trains offer amenities like reclining seats or even sleeping compartments for ultimate comfort. And for people with health concerns like high blood pressure, train travel can be a much less stressful option.","Honestly, I find myself drawn to different modes of travel depending on the situation. For shorter trips, I enjoy the convenience and speed of driving my own car. However, for longer distances, I favor train travel. I find the opportunity to relax, enjoy the views, and even catch up on some reading during the journey incredibly appealing. Plus, it's a more sustainable choice for the environment. Ultimately, it's about finding the best balance between time, cost, comfort, and my environmental impact."],"part2":"One of the most satisfying achievements in my life was when I finally bought my first car. It wasn't just about acquiring a vehicle; it represented a culmination of hard work, financial discipline, and a significant step toward independence. From a young age, I'd always envisioned myself driving, exploring new places, and having the freedom to create my own adventures. My father played a pivotal role in shaping my journey. He instilled in me the value of financial responsibility and encouraged me to be proactive in achieving my goals. He didn't just hand me the keys; he guided me through the process, teaching me how to research different models, negotiate with dealerships, and even understand the intricacies of car insurance. It was a steep learning curve, but his unwavering support and pragmatic advice made the entire experience enriching. When I finally signed the papers and drove my car home, I felt an overwhelming sense of accomplishment. It wasn't just about the car itself, but about the personal growth I experienced. I realized that with determination and a clear vision, I could achieve anything I set my mind to. It was a pivotal moment that instilled in me a confidence I carry with me to this day. The journey to acquiring my first car wasn't just about acquiring a vehicle, it was about becoming a more independent, responsible, and self-assured individual.","part3":"When students have their phones with them, it's really hard for them to concentrate on their lessons. They're constantly checking messages, scrolling through social media, or playing games. Banning phones would mean students would pay more attention in class, listen to their teachers, and take better notes. This would help them learn more effectively and get better grades. In addition, when students are glued to their phones, they miss out on opportunities to do other things, like playing sports, joining clubs, or spending time with friends. A ban on phones would encourage students to be more active, social, and involved in school life. This would help them develop their social skills, get more exercise, and learn new things outside of the classroom. Finally, constant use of smartphones can lead to eye strain, headaches, and even sleep problems. A ban on phones in school would mean students would spend less time staring at screens, which could improve their overall health and well-being. Despite these plus sides of banning, smartphones can be valuable tools for learning. Students can use them to research information, access educational apps, and even take notes electronically. A ban on phones would restrict their access to these resources, potentially hindering their learning process and putting them at a disadvantage compared to students who have access to these technologies outside of school. Smartphones are essential for communication, especially in emergencies. Banning them could make it harder for students to contact their parents, guardians, or other emergency services if needed. It could also limit their ability to communicate with friends and family in case of unforeseen circumstances. Furthermore, while there are valid concerns about distractions, smartphones can also be utilized as valuable tools for learning. Students can use educational apps, access online resources, or even participate in interactive learning activities through their phones. A blanket ban on phones would disregard these potential benefits and hinder the possibilities for incorporating technology into modern education."}},{"id":"mb07","title":"Mock Book · Mock 7","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Do you like listening to music?","What kind of weather don't you like?","What do you do after work or school?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of doing sport?","Which is better: doing sport indoors or outdoors?"],"part1_2_images":["mb07_p12_1.jpg","mb07_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a team project that you worked on.","What was it and what did you do?","How did you feel about it?"],"part2_image":"mb07_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Online education is better than offline education.","for":["Online education offers a greater degree of flexibility","Online platforms offer an abundance of resources","Online education is often a more cost-effective alternative to traditional education"],"against":["Offline education fosters direct interaction between students and teachers","Traditional classrooms provide a structured learning environment with set schedules and routines","Offline education gives students opportunities to build meaningful relationships"]},"model":{"part1_1":["Oh absolutely! Music is a huge part of my life. I find it really relaxing to unwind with some tunes after a long day. I especially enjoy listening to soul music, as it is stress reliever activity before going to sleep. And of course, I love going to concerts and live performances whenever I can.","Well, I'm not a huge fan of extremely humid weather. It just feels stifling and uncomfortable. I also find it hard to concentrate when it's unbearably hot. I much prefer cooler temperatures and a bit of a breeze. There's nothing quite like a crisp autumn day, for instance.","After work or school, I usually try to de-stress and recharge. I might catch up with friends, grab a bite to eat, or just relax at home. Sometimes I'll indulge in a hobby, like [mention your hobby and briefly explain why you enjoy it]. It's important for me to have some time to unwind and do things I enjoy before the next day begins."],"part1_2":["The images present two different ways of running to keep fit. While the first one features a woman who has a small backpack is running amidst breathtaking mountain scenery. This method helps runner to feel the nature and capture its beauty. In contrast, the second picture shows a woman running on the designated running track in the gym. This method is ideal for city dwellers who may lack access to outdoor running routes to take care of their health.","There are tons of benefits to engaging in sports! First and foremost, it's fantastic for physical health. It strengthens muscles, improves cardiovascular fitness, and helps maintain a healthy weight. But it's not just about the body, it's also great for mental well-being. Sports can boost mood, reduce stress, and even improve sleep quality. Plus, being involved in a team or group can foster a sense of camaraderie and social interaction. So, it's a win-win all around!","Honestly, I think it depends on the individual's preferences and circumstances. I personally enjoy the feeling of fresh air and sunshine when exercising outdoors, and I love the chance to explore different trails or parks. However, indoor sports can be great too, especially when the weather is bad or if you need a controlled environment. Gyms offer a lot of variety and professional guidance. Ultimately, it comes down to what motivates you to get moving."],"part2":"One of the most impactful team projects I participated in was during my environmental studies class. We were tasked with researching and debating a pressing global issue related to the worsening state of nature. Our group chose to focus on the alarming increase in plastic pollution, particularly in our oceans. My role in the team was to delve into the scientific research surrounding plastic pollution, focusing on its impact on marine life, ecosystems, and even human health. We uncovered staggering statistics about the sheer volume of plastic entering our oceans each year, and the devastating consequences for seabirds, marine mammals, and coral reefs. It was truly eye-opening to see the scale of the problem and how it was affecting our planet in such profound ways. We then used this research to develop a compelling debate presentation. We presented a series of arguments highlighting the urgency of the issue, the consequences of inaction, and the potential solutions. We explored various approaches, from individual lifestyle changes to policy initiatives aimed at reducing plastic production and promoting sustainable alternatives. During the debate, we engaged in constructive dialogue with other teams, challenging each other's perspectives and building upon shared understandings. The experience was truly impactful. It not only deepened my understanding of the complex environmental challenges we face, but it also ignited a passion for finding solutions. It was incredibly motivating to work alongside my teammates, collaborating to present a well-researched and engaging argument. The debate itself was a powerful learning experience, fostering critical thinking and highlighting the importance of responsible environmental stewardship. It made me realize that even small actions can have a significant impact, and it instilled in me a sense of urgency to become an advocate for environmental protection.","part3":"Admittedly, online studying can offer a wide range of possibilities unlike traditional education. Firstly, it offers a greater degree of flexibility. Students can choose when and where to study, which is especially helpful for those who have jobs or family commitments. This means they can learn at their own pace, making it easier to balance their studies with other responsibilities. Secondly, online platforms provide an abundance of resources. Students have access to video lectures, interactive quizzes, and discussion forums, which can cater to different learning styles. This variety helps students understand the material better and keeps them engaged in their studies. Finally, online education is often more cost-effective than traditional education. Students save money on commuting, housing, and other campus-related expenses. Additionally, many online courses have lower tuition fees, making education more accessible to a wider range of people. On the other hand, offline education has its own advantages that make it a better option for some students. One major benefit is that it fosters direct interaction between students and teachers. In a classroom setting, students can ask questions immediately and receive feedback, which can enhance their understanding of the subject matter. Moreover, traditional classrooms provide a structured learning environment. With set schedules and routines, students are more likely to stay focused and organized. This structure can help those who might struggle with self-discipline when studying online. Lastly, offline education allows students to build meaningful relationships with their peers and instructors. These connections can lead to collaborative learning experiences and networking opportunities that are often harder to achieve in an online format."}},{"id":"mb08","title":"Mock Book · Mock 8","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Who was your first teacher?","What is your favorite number?","Tell me about your hometown."],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of indoor activities?","Why do children like indoor activities?"],"part1_2_images":["mb08_p12_1.jpg","mb08_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a time when you tried to do something but failed.","When was it and what did you try to do?","Why were you not successful in doing it?"],"part2_image":"mb08_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Gardening should be taught at school.","for":["Spending time in a garden can be incredibly relaxing for pupils","Students can learn about planting and growing food","Gardening fosters an appreciation for the natural world"],"against":["Schools already have packed schedules, and adding another subject can be challenging","Not all schools have suitable outdoor space for a garden","While some students might find gardening engaging, others may not be interested in it"]},"model":{"part1_1":["My first teacher was a kind and patient woman named Mrs. Smith. She taught me in kindergarten, and I remember her fondly for her colourful classroom and the fun activities she planned. She really helped to instill a love of learning in me, and I still remember some of the things she taught us, like the alphabet and basic counting. I think it's important to have a good first teacher because it can set the stage for a positive learning experience later on.","My favorite number is 7. It's the number I was born on, so it holds a special significance for me. It also happens to be a lucky number in my culture, which I always find reassuring. I always feel a bit more optimistic when I see the number 7 pop up, even in seemingly random places","My hometown is Rishtan, located in Fergana. It's medium sized area with historical landmarks, natural beauty, bustling markets. I love my hometown for its friendly people, peaceful atmosphere, vibrant culture. In one words, It's a great place to grow up and a place I'm proud to call home."],"part1_2":["Both pictures present children who are engaging in indoor and outdoor activities. As for the first one, some young children are immersing in the game around the table. Indoor games can ensure that young ones can be occupied with physical activities at any time regardless of the weather conditions. While in the second picture, some children are playing a ball in the yard. Outdoor interactions with peers can help children build good social skills.","Indoor activities offer a number of advantages, especially in certain climates or during specific seasons. One major benefit is protection from the elements. Whether it's scorching heat, pouring rain, or biting cold, indoor activities provide a comfortable and controlled environment. This can be particularly important for people with health concerns or young children who are more sensitive to extreme weather.","Children, with their boundless energy and curiosity, often find indoor activities captivating. One reason is that many indoor spaces are specifically designed to entertain and stimulate young minds. Playgrounds, museums, and even shopping malls offer exciting attractions that keep children engaged and entertained. Another plus side is that Indoor spaces are also often temperature-controlled, providing comfort and protection for little ones."],"part2":"I remember vividly the time I first took the IELTS exam. I was aiming for a Band 7 overall, which I knew would open up a lot of opportunities for me. I diligently studied for months, focusing on all four skills - listening, reading, writing, and speaking. I even joined a preparation course and practiced with past exam papers. I felt confident going into the test, but unfortunately, I didn't achieve my desired score. I fell short in the writing section, only scoring a Band 6.5. It was a huge disappointment, and I was disheartened. Analyzing my results, I realized that my biggest weakness was structuring my essays and using more complex vocabulary effectively. I had a good grasp of grammar and sentence structure, but my essays lacked a strong flow and didn't demonstrate a sophisticated use of language. The experience was a valuable lesson for me. I realized that simply studying the material wasn't enough. I needed to develop a more strategic approach, focusing on areas where I struggled. I signed up for additional writing lessons, studied specific vocabulary related to academic writing, and practiced writing different essay types under timed conditions. This time, I focused on developing strong arguments, clear paragraphing, and using a wider range of vocabulary to express my ideas. It wasn't an easy process, but I eventually achieved my goal of a Band 7 overall. This experience taught me the importance of identifying your weaknesses, seeking help where necessary, and putting in the hard work to improve.","part3":"Admittedly, if gardening is taught at school, this can bring a number of benefits. One compelling argument for incorporating gardening into school curricula is its potential to foster a sense of well-being and connection to nature. Spending time in a garden can be incredibly relaxing for pupils, providing a much-needed respite from the often stressful environment of the classroom. The act of nurturing plants, observing their growth, and reaping the rewards of their labor can be deeply rewarding, cultivating patience, focus, and a sense of accomplishment. Furthermore, by engaging in hands-on activities in a natural setting, students can develop a greater appreciation for the environment, understand the importance of sustainability, and learn practical skills for cultivating healthy food sources. However, practical considerations may hinder the implementation of gardening programs in schools. A primary concern is the already packed schedules of most schools, with limited time available for additional subjects. Adding another subject, especially one that requires outdoor access and ongoing maintenance, could prove challenging, potentially displacing existing programs or extracurricular activities. Furthermore, not all schools have suitable outdoor space for a garden, particularly in urban areas where land is scarce. Even if space is available, ensuring the necessary resources, such as tools, materials, and ongoing maintenance, can be a significant financial burden. Ultimately, the success of a school garden depends on the commitment of both teachers and students, and not all pupils may find gardening engaging, leading to potential disinterest and lack of participation."}},{"id":"mb09","title":"Mock Book · Mock 9","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["What kind of movies do you like?","What is your favorite type of weather?","What do you eat for breakfast?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","Why do some people prefer private cars?","Why do other people prefer public transport?"],"part1_2_images":["mb09_p12_1.jpg","mb09_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a new skill you would like to learn.","What is it and why do you need it?","What should you do to learn it?"],"part2_image":"mb09_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"All countries should adopt a single global language.","for":["This would eliminate language barriers","This can lead to better cultural exchange and understanding","No need for translation services and language learning"],"against":["This can lead to the erosion of cultures and local languages","Not all individuals have the same level of access to education","It would take many years for every country's population to master a global language"]},"model":{"part1_1":["I'm a big fan of movies that transport me to another world, you know, the kind that really captivate my imagination. I'm particularly drawn to historical dramas, especially those that explore complex characters and pivotal moments in history. For example, I recently watched a film about the French Revolution, and it really made me think about the social and political forces at play. I also enjoy a good thriller, as long as it keeps me on the edge of my seat and doesn't rely on jump scares. A well-crafted thriller can be incredibly suspenseful and thought-provoking.","That's a tough one, as I enjoy different weather for different reasons. I suppose my favorite would have to be a crisp autumn day, with clear blue skies and just a hint of a chill in the air. It's the perfect weather for taking a long walk in the park, enjoying the changing colors of the leaves, and the fresh smell of the air. Of course, a warm summer evening with a gentle breeze is also pretty amazing for relaxing outdoors and enjoying the long daylight hours.","My breakfast routine varies depending on my schedule, but I always try to start the day with something nourishing. On weekdays, I usually opt for a quick and easy breakfast of yogurt with granola and fruit. It's packed with protein and fiber, which helps me feel full and energized until lunchtime. On weekends, I have more time to experiment, so I might make a smoothie with spinach, banana, and berries, or maybe some avocado toast with a poached egg. I'm trying to be mindful of my diet, so I always aim for a balanced breakfast that includes a good mix of carbohydrates, protein, and healthy fats."],"part1_2":["These two pictures offer contrasting perspectives on commuting. The first image captures a family traveling comfortably in their own car, suggesting a sense of autonomy and control over their journey. This mode of transport often prioritizes speed and privacy, allowing for a more personalized experience. In contrast, the second picture depicts a group of passengers on a bus, engaged in lively conversation, suggesting a sense of community and connection. Public transport, though potentially less convenient in terms of time and flexibility, is a cost-effective and reliable option, providing accessibility to a wider segment of the population.","People prefer private cars for several reasons, I think. One key factor is convenience. It offers flexibility in terms of scheduling and destination. You can go wherever you want, whenever you want, without relying on a fixed timetable or route. Also, comfort and privacy are often cited as advantages. You can control the temperature, listen to your own music, and avoid the potential crowds on public transport. Of course, safety and security are also important for some people, especially if they are traveling with young children or valuable belongings","There are a lot of benefits to using public transport, especially in busy urban areas. Cost is a major one, as it's usually much cheaper than owning and running a car. It's also environmentally friendly, as it reduces traffic congestion and carbon emissions. Another benefit is reduced stress, especially for commuters who can relax and read or use their phones while traveling. In some cities, it's simply more efficient to get around by public transport, as it's often faster than driving in heavy traffic."],"part2":"If I could learn a new skill, it would be to master the English language. While I can communicate in English fairly well, I want to achieve a much higher level of fluency and proficiency. For me, it's not just about being able to understand and speak, but also about confidently engaging in complex conversations, expressing myself more creatively, and expanding my professional opportunities. My goal is to become more comfortable using a wider range of vocabulary and grammar, and to be able to express myself more clearly and effectively. This would open doors to new career paths, enable me to connect with people from diverse backgrounds, and allow me to enjoy literature, movies, and music in English to a greater degree. To achieve this, I'd need to immerse myself in the language. I'd start by reading English books and articles regularly, focusing on a variety of genres. I'd also listen to English podcasts and watch movies and TV shows with subtitles. I'd make a conscious effort to speak English whenever possible, even if it means practicing with friends or family. I'd enroll in an online English course to enhance my grammar and vocabulary, and I'd look for opportunities to join English-speaking groups or clubs. I'm confident that with consistent dedication, I can achieve fluency in English and unlock a world of possibilities.","part3":"The idea of adopting a single global language is a compelling one, offering several potential advantages. It would undoubtedly break down communication barriers, fostering smoother collaboration and understanding between individuals and nations. Imagine the efficiency gained in business negotiations, diplomatic talks, and even everyday travel, without the need for translation services. This could also lead to a more unified global community, promoting cultural exchange and reducing misunderstandings. Furthermore, the vast resources currently spent on language learning and translation could be redirected towards other vital areas. However, this seemingly utopian scenario also presents significant challenges. The adoption of a single language could lead to the erosion of cultural diversity, with minority languages and traditions fading away. The process of learning a new language, particularly for older generations, might be arduous and time-consuming. Furthermore, equitable access to language education would be crucial to ensure that everyone has the opportunity to participate in this new linguistic landscape. The potential for social inequality and exclusion could arise if certain groups lack the resources or access to learn the global language. Ultimately, while a single global language has its merits, the potential consequences for cultural diversity and inclusivity cannot be ignored."}},{"id":"mb10","title":"Mock Book · Mock 10","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["What do you do on the weekends?","Do you live in a house or flat?","What kind of movies do you like?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of family travelling?","Which types of trip would you prefer?"],"part1_2_images":["mb10_p12_1.jpg","mb10_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a time when you shared a secret with others.","Describe the situation that led to sharing the secret.","Mention the people involved in the secret-sharing and the consequences."],"part2_image":"mb10_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Owning a pet has more advantages than disadvantages.","for":["Pets can provide companionship and emotional support","Owning a pet can encourage you to be more active","Caring for a pet teaches important life skills"],"against":["Owning a pet means extra expenses","Pets need a lot of attention and care","Owning a pet can limit your lifestyle choices"]},"model":{"part1_1":["My weekends are usually a mix of relaxing activities and catching up on things I don't have time for during the week. I love to spend time with friends, so we often go out for brunch or to see a movie. And, of course, I always make sure to allocate some time for reading, as I find it incredibly relaxing and stimulating. It's important for me to unwind and recharge after a busy week, and my weekends are a perfect opportunity to do just that.","I live in a cozy flat in the heart of the city. It's a two-bedroom apartment on the third floor, and I really love the vibrant energy of living close to everything. I enjoy having easy access to shops, restaurants, and cultural events, and being able to walk to most places. Although it's a bit noisy sometimes, I wouldn't trade the convenience and community feel for anything. Plus, having a balcony where I can enjoy a cup of coffee in the morning is a real perk.","I'm a big fan of movies that really draw me in and make me think. I love well-crafted stories with compelling characters and thought-provoking themes. I'm particularly drawn to independent films and foreign cinema, as they often explore unique perspectives and tackle issues that mainstream movies might shy away from. Of course, I also enjoy a good action movie or comedy when I'm looking for something lighter and more entertaining. But for me, the most satisfying movies are the ones that leave a lasting impression and spark conversations."],"part1_2":["Both pictures compare family travelling and solo travelling. As for the first one, an immediate family, a little daughter with her parents, is in the airport, holding their trip tickets. All of them are excited as the smiles on their faces expose. Family trip is quite fun to have a quality time together, and it also helps make family ties stronger. In contrast, the second picture shows a woman traveling by herself, holding a map of the area. Travelling alone has also advantages, giving travellers a chance of relieving their stress, doing what they want.","Family travel offers a unique set of advantages, primarily the opportunity to strengthen family bonds and create lasting memories. It allows families to experience new cultures together, share adventures, and learn from one another in a way that's not possible in everyday life. It's also a chance to escape the routine and create shared experiences that everyone can cherish for years to come. For example, witnessing the awe in a child's eyes as they see a majestic mountain range or the laughter shared around a campfire during a camping trip creates priceless moments that solidify family connections.","While I enjoy the companionship of others on trips, I find myself drawn to solo travel more often. It allows me to really get to know myself better, to make decisions based solely on my own interests, and to truly appreciate the solitude. There's a certain freedom and independence that comes with exploring a new place on my own terms. I can spend as much time as I want in a museum or wander off the beaten path without feeling pressured to keep up with a group. Of course, sharing adventures with loved ones is also incredibly rewarding, but I find that solo travel provides a unique opportunity for personal growth and self-discovery."],"part2":"I’d like to talk about a time when I shared a secret with my close friends. This happened about a year ago when I was planning a surprise birthday party for my best friend, Sarah. I wanted it to be a big surprise, but I realized I couldn’t do it alone. So, I decided to share the secret with a few of our mutual friends. The situation started when I found out that Sarah was feeling a bit down because she thought nobody remembered her birthday. I thought it would be a great idea to organize a surprise party to cheer her up. I first talked to my friend Mark and then included two other friends, Lisa and Tom. We all agreed that we wanted to make it special for her. When I shared the secret with them, they were really excited and immediately started brainstorming ideas. However, there was a bit of pressure because we had to keep it a secret from Sarah. We planned everything carefully, from the decorations to the cake, and decided to invite her family and some close friends. The consequences of sharing this secret were mostly positive. We managed to pull off the surprise party successfully, and Sarah was genuinely shocked and thrilled when she walked in. It brought us all closer together as we worked as a team to make it happen. However, there was a moment of panic when one of our friends accidentally mentioned the word \"party\" in front of Sarah, but luckily she didn’t catch on. In the end, sharing the secret not only made the party a success but also strengthened our friendship. It taught me that sometimes sharing a secret can lead to wonderful experiences and that teamwork is really important in making things happen.","part3":"Raising a pet at home has its own certain pros and cons. As for the advantages, pets can provide a sense of companionship and emotional support, especially for people who live alone or have limited social interaction. They can reduce stress and anxiety, offer a sense of purpose and routine, and provide unconditional love and affection. Moreover, owning a pet, especially a dog, encourages a more active lifestyle. Regular walks, playtime, and outdoor activities not only benefit the pet's health but also keep the owner physically fit. This increased activity can lead to better overall health, helping to reduce stress and improve mood. In addition, caring for a pet teaches important life skills such as responsibility, empathy, and patience. Pet owners learn to meet the needs of another living being, which can foster a greater understanding of caring for others. This experience is particularly valuable for children, as it helps them develop nurturing qualities and a sense of accountability. However, owning a pet can be expensive. You need to pay for food, vet bills, grooming, and toys. Some animals, like dogs, require specialized training or daycare, which can add to the costs. This can be a significant financial burden, especially for those on a tight budget. In addition, pets need a lot of attention and care. You need to feed them, walk them, play with them, and take them to the vet. This can be challenging for busy people or those with limited free time. It can also affect your social life, as you may need to decline invitations or rearrange your schedule to accommodate your pet's needs. Another minus side is that owning a pet can limit your lifestyle choices. You might not be able to travel as freely, especially if you're going somewhere that doesn't allow pets. You also might need to make adjustments to your home environment to accommodate your pet, such as installing a pet door or purchasing pet-friendly furniture. This can be a challenge for those who are accustomed to a more flexible and spontaneous lifestyle."}},{"id":"mb11","title":"Mock Book · Mock 11","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Tell me about your room.","Do you often make friends when traveling?","Do you have many friends?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of doing shopping with friends?","Do you usually shop alone or with others?"],"part1_2_images":["mb11_p12_1.jpg","mb11_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a problem you solved.","What obstacles did you face?","What did you learn from the experience?"],"part2_image":"mb11_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Cameras should be required in public areas.","for":["The presence of cameras can deter criminal activity","Cameras can provide valuable evidence in the event of a crime","Increased community trust and transparency"],"against":["Cameras in public spaces can lead to concerns about privacy","Cameras can be misused by those who have access to the footage","Installing and maintaining surveillance cameras can be expensive"]},"model":{"part1_1":["My room is my sanctuary! It's a bit small, but I've made it my own. It's got a comfy bed, a large desk where I do my work, and lots of bookshelves. I like to keep it tidy, but I also have some quirky decorations that make it feel personal.","I've been lucky enough to meet some really interesting people while traveling. It's easier to connect with people when you're both outside your comfort zones and experiencing something new. I usually strike up conversations with locals, and often those turn into friendships. It's a great way to learn about different cultures.","I wouldn't say I have a *huge* circle of friends, but I do have a few close friends who I consider to be very important to me. Quality over quantity, you know? We've been friends for a long time, and we share a lot in common. We enjoy doing things together, like going to concerts, trying new restaurants, or just hanging out at home and having deep conversations. Even though we don't see each other every day, I know I can always count on them for support and encouragement. I value the connections I have with them deeply, and that's what truly matters to me."],"part1_2":["The two photos present contrasting scenes of clothing shopping. In the first image, we see a group of three women engaged in a very social and interactive shopping experience. They seem to be helping one another choose an outfit, likely for a special occasion, as they meticulously check the fit, length, and color of the garment. The interaction between them suggests a close-knit friendship, as they offer advice and collaborate on finding the perfect look. The second picture, on the other hand, showcases a solitary shopping experience. A woman is browsing the racks alone, carefully examining the price tags and the quality of the clothing. Her body language conveys a sense of focus and independence, as she makes her choices without external influence.","Shopping with friends is a really fun way to spend time together. You can bounce ideas off each other, get honest opinions on different styles, and maybe even find some great deals together! Plus, it's always nice to have someone to share the excitement of finding a new outfit with. Sometimes, having a friend's perspective can give you the confidence to try something you might not normally consider, and it can even spark some creative ideas for how to style your new clothes.","I tend to prefer shopping alone, but I don't mind going with a friend occasionally. When I'm shopping alone, I can browse at my own pace and focus on finding exactly what I'm looking for. I'm not easily influenced by trends or peer pressure, so I can make my own choices without feeling rushed or pressured. However, it's always fun to get a different perspective when shopping with a friend. It's like a mini fashion show! Ultimately, I enjoy both experiences and I think it's important to find the right balance."],"part2":"A few months ago, I had this big problem with my car. It started making this strange rattling noise, and it was getting worse every time I drove it. I was really worried because I needed my car to get to work and for other daily activities. At first, I tried to figure out the problem myself, but I'm not very mechanically inclined, so that didn't work out too well. I even tried searching online for solutions, but I couldn't find anything that matched the specific sound my car was making. One of the biggest obstacles I faced was the sheer lack of knowledge about car mechanics. I had no idea what was causing the problem, and I was afraid of making things worse by trying to fix it myself. I also had to deal with the stress of not knowing how long it would take to get my car fixed and the inconvenience of having to rely on other forms of transportation. Eventually, I decided to take my car to a mechanic. It turned out to be a loose part in the exhaust system, and the mechanic fixed it within a couple of hours. It was a relief to have it fixed, but the experience taught me a valuable lesson about the importance of seeking help when I need it. I realized that I don't have to be an expert in everything, and it's okay to ask for help when I'm struggling with something. This experience also made me appreciate the value of having a reliable car and the convenience it provides. From now on, I'll make sure to get regular maintenance checks for my car, and I won't hesitate to take it to a mechanic if I notice any unusual noises or problems.","part3":"If surveillance cameras are installed in community zones, this can bring up both pros and cons sides. On the one hand, the presence of cameras can deter criminal activity, as potential offenders may think twice before committing a crime if they know they are being monitored. This can lead to a reduction in incidents such as theft, vandalism, and violence, contributing to a safer environment for everyone. And Cameras can provide valuable evidence in the event of a crime. Video footage can help law enforcement identify suspects, understand the sequence of events, and gather crucial information that may not be available through eyewitness accounts alone. This can lead to quicker resolutions of cases and increased accountability. In addition, the implementation of cameras in public areas can foster a sense of security among community members. When people feel that their safety is being prioritized and that there is transparency in public spaces, it can enhance trust in local authorities and law enforcement. This can encourage community engagement and cooperation in maintaining safety and order. On the other hand, the presence of cameras in public spaces can lead to concerns about privacy. Individuals may feel uncomfortable knowing they are constantly being monitored, which can create a sense of surveillance that infringes on personal freedoms and rights. Moreover, cameras can be misused by those who have access to the footage. This could lead to unauthorized surveillance, harassment, or discrimination against certain individuals or groups. There is also the risk of data breaches, where sensitive footage could be accessed and exploited by malicious actors. Another drawback of this, installing and maintaining surveillance cameras can be expensive. This includes the costs of purchasing equipment, installation, ongoing maintenance, and storage of video footage. These funds might be better allocated to other community safety measures or social programs."}},{"id":"mb12","title":"Mock Book · Mock 12","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["How much time do you spend on the internet?","Who is your favorite singer?","What do you do in the evening?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the benefits of eating alone?","What are the benefits of eating with friends?"],"part1_2_images":["mb12_p12_1.jpg","mb12_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a movie that you watched recently.","When and where did you watch it?","Did you like it? Why?"],"part2_image":"mb12_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Schools should separate children according to their ability.","for":["Students will be less self-conscious about their performance","Teachers can focus their methods and materials more easily","Faster learners are not held back by slower ones"],"against":["Negative labelling and limited opportunities","Reduced social interaction and collaboration","Unfairness and inequality"]},"model":{"part1_1":["I spend quite a bit of time on the internet, probably around three to four hours a day. Most of this time is spent on social media, browsing news websites, and sometimes watching videos. I find it useful for staying connected with friends and family, especially since many of them live far away. However, I try to limit my time online in the evenings so that I can focus on other activities like reading or spending time with my family.","My favorite singer is Ed Sheeran. I really like his music because it has a lot of emotion and tells great stories. His songs are catchy, and I enjoy how he mixes different styles, like pop and folk. I’ve listened to many of his albums, and I find that his lyrics often resonate with my own experiences. Whenever I feel stressed or need to relax, I put on his music, and it always helps me feel better.","In the evening, I usually have a routine that helps me unwind after a long day. First, I like to have dinner with my family, which is a great time to catch up and talk about our day. After that, I might watch a movie or a TV show for some entertainment. Sometimes, I also read a book or listen to music before going to bed. I think having this time in the evening is important for relaxing and recharging for the next day."],"part1_2":["Both pictures show different lunch experiences. In the first photo, a woman is sitting alone in a cafeteria, looking thoughtful. It seems like she is lost in her own thoughts. In contrast, the second picture shows a group of four women enjoying lunch together, chatting and laughing. This creates a lively and friendly atmosphere. Overall, these images highlight how lunch can be a solitary moment or a time for socializing with friends.","Eating alone can have several benefits. Firstly, it allows for personal reflection and quiet time. When you eat by yourself, you can think about your day or enjoy your meal without distractions. Secondly, eating alone gives you the freedom to choose what you want to eat without considering anyone else's preferences. This means you can try new foods or enjoy your favorite dishes without compromise. Lastly, it can be a good way to recharge, especially for people who feel overwhelmed by social interactions","Eating with friends has many advantages. One of the main benefits is the social aspect; sharing a meal can strengthen relationships and create lasting memories. When friends gather to eat, they often share stories and laughter, which can improve mood and reduce stress. Additionally, eating together can encourage healthier eating habits, as friends may motivate each other to make better food choices."],"part2":"I recently watched \"The Pursuit of Happiness,\" a film that deeply impacted me. I saw it a few weeks ago at home, streaming it on a quiet Sunday evening. I’d heard about its powerful story, but seeing it firsthand was truly moving. The film follows Chris Gardner, a struggling salesman who is battling homelessness while trying to secure a coveted internship at a prestigious brokerage firm. Will Smith's performance is phenomenal, conveying the immense pressure and emotional toll of his circumstances with heartbreaking realism. What struck me most was the film's unflinching portrayal of poverty and the relentless struggle for self-improvement. Despite facing incredible adversity – including eviction and the constant worry for his young son's well-being – Chris Gardner never gives up hope. His determination and unwavering love for his son are truly inspiring. While it's undoubtedly a difficult watch at times, the film offers a message of hope and resilience that is both uplifting and unforgettable. The emotional weight of the story is balanced by moments of tenderness and humor, making it a truly captivating and emotionally resonant experience. It’s a film I'll likely rewatch again sometime soon.","part3":"There are a number of advantages of dividing students into groups coming from their abilities. When students are grouped with peers of similar abilities, they're more likely to feel a sense of belonging and less self-conscious about their performance. This improved social dynamic fosters greater engagement in learning activities. In addition, Ability grouping allows teachers to adapt their teaching methods and pace to the specific needs and learning styles of each group. Faster learners aren't held back by slower ones, preventing boredom and fostering a sense of accomplishment. Conversely, slower learners receive more focused attention and support, improving their understanding and confidence. This targeted approach maximizes individual progress, ensuring that each student is challenged appropriately and can reach their full potential. Furthermore, Students in higher ability groups are less likely to feel constrained by slower peers, enabling them to progress at their own pace and take intellectual risks, develop critical thinking by doing difficult tasks according to their performance. On the other hand, Putting kids into \"high\" or \"low\" groups can create labels that stick. Children in lower groups might feel less confident and believe they can't achieve as much, even if they could. This can limit their chances to learn and grow. Those in higher groups might become complacent, thinking they don't need to try hard. Reduced Social Interaction and Collaboration: Grouping by ability can mean kids only interact with others at a similar level. This misses out on the benefits of learning from and working with people with different strengths and perspectives. It can also create divisions and misunderstandings between groups. Ability grouping doesn't always fairly reflect a child's true potential. Factors like background, teaching quality, and learning styles can affect test scores and placement. This can unfairly disadvantage certain students, making it harder for them to succeed and widening the gap between different groups."}},{"id":"mb13","title":"Mock Book · Mock 13","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["What do you do on weekends?","How often do you watch TV?","Who is your best friend?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the advantages of having salad?","What are the disadvantages of eating junk food?"],"part1_2_images":["mb13_p12_1.jpg","mb13_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a time when you felt happy.","Why is it important to have a good mood?","Can money make people happy?"],"part2_image":"mb13_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"School days should start later.","for":["Improved academic performance","Enhanced physical and mental health","Increased safety and fewer accidents"],"against":["Logistical challenges and disruption","Less time for extracurricular activities","Potentially less time for family activities and chores"]},"model":{"part1_1":["On weekends, I usually like to relax and spend time with my family and friends. I often go out for lunch or dinner, and sometimes we watch movies together. I also enjoy doing some outdoor activities, like hiking or biking, especially if the weather is nice. Additionally, I try to catch up on reading or work on personal projects that I don’t have time for during the week.","I watch TV a few times a week, usually in the evenings after work. I enjoy watching a mix of shows, including dramas and documentaries. Usually, I watch football matches on weekends when I have more free time. However, I try not to spend too much time in front of the screen, as I prefer to engage in other activities like reading or exercising.","My best friend is Xushnud I’ve known since high school, and we have a lot in common. We enjoy similar hobbies, like traveling and trying new restaurants. We support each other through good times and bad, and I really appreciate having him in my life. We often meet up on weekends to catch up and have fun together."],"part1_2":["In these photos, we can see two different eating experiences. The first photo shows a woman enjoying a healthy salad along with some mineral water. This suggests she is focused on eating nutritious food. In contrast, the second photo features three teenagers sharing traditional hamburgers and having a fun conversation. This indicates a more casual and social dining experience.","One major advantage of having salads is that they are packed with essential nutrients like vitamins and antioxidants. They also provide a good amount of fiber, which aids in digestion and helps maintain a healthy weight. Additionally, salads are versatile and can be customized with various ingredients to suit different tastes.","ne significant disadvantage of eating junk food is its high calorie content combined with low nutritional value. Regular consumption can lead to weight gain and increase the risk of chronic diseases such as diabetes and heart disease. Moreover, junk food often contains high levels of unhealthy fats, sugars, and preservatives, which can negatively impact overall health."],"part2":"I felt really happy last summer when I went on a trip with my friends to the beach. We spent the whole day swimming, playing volleyball, and just relaxing under the sun. One moment that stands out is when we had a picnic together and laughed a lot over funny stories. The weather was perfect, and we all felt carefree. Being with my friends made me feel connected and joyful and it was one of those days where everything seemed perfect. Having a good mood is important because it affects how we interact with others and handle daily challenges. When we feel happy, we are more likely to be kind and supportive to our friends and family. A good mood also helps us think clearly and make better decisions. For example, when I am in a good mood, I can focus better at work or school, and I am more motivated to achieve my goals. Overall, a positive mood contributes to our well-being and makes life more enjoyable. Money can make people happy to some extent, but it is not the only factor that brings happiness. Having enough money can help meet basic needs like food, shelter, and healthcare, which definitely contributes to overall happiness. However, once those needs are met, other things like relationships, experiences, and personal fulfillment become more important. I think that while money can provide comfort and security, true happiness often comes from meaningful connections with others and doing things that we love.","part3":"If school days commence later, this will bring about both some advantages and disadvantages at the same time. On the one hand, later school start times align better with teenagers' natural sleep-wake cycles, leading to increased alertness, concentration, and better cognitive function in class. This translates to improved academic performance, higher test scores, and reduced absenteeism .Another plus side is that adequate sleep is crucial for physical and mental well-being. Later start times allow teenagers to get the necessary sleep, reducing the risk of obesity, depression, anxiety, and other health issues often linked to sleep deprivation. This leads to happier, healthier students, better equipped to learn. Furthermore, teenagers' sleep patterns are biologically different from those of younger children or adults. Sleep-deprived teenagers are more prone to accidents and injuries, whether on the way to school, during school activities, or even at home. Later start times contribute to increased safety by reducing the risk of drowsy driving and other accidents. However, the negative sides of this approach should be also taken into account. First and foremost, shifting school start times requires significant adjustments to school schedules, bus routes, after-school activities, and the work schedules of parents and caregivers. This can lead to logistical difficulties, increased costs, and potential disruption to the daily routines of families and communities. In addition, later school start times may encroach on the time available for extracurricular activities, sports practices, and other enriching pursuits. This can negatively impact students' participation in these activities, potentially limiting their social development and opportunities for personal growth. Finally, with a later school day, the time available for family meals, homework assistance, and household chores might be reduced. This could strain family dynamics and impact students' responsibilities at home, potentially affecting their sense of contribution and responsibility."}},{"id":"mb14","title":"Mock Book · Mock 14","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Do you like flowers?","Tell me about your first teacher.","What kind of books do you like to read?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the challenges of travelling by plane?","What are the benefits of travelling by train?"],"part1_2_images":["mb14_p12_1.jpg","mb14_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a time when you had a disagreement with someone.","When do people usually argue with each other?","What suggestions can you give to solve disagreements?"],"part2_image":"mb14_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"Using the internet should be banned for those under 16.","for":["Better protection from online harms","Improved focus on education and development","More parental control and family interaction"],"against":["Limited access to educational resources and opportunities","Hindered social and emotional development","Difficulty in preparing for the digital age"]},"model":{"part1_1":["Yes, I appreciate flowers. I find them aesthetically pleasing; the variety of colors, shapes, and fragrances is captivating. I especially enjoy seeing them in gardens or wild meadows, where they contribute to the overall beauty of the natural landscape. While I don’t have a deep knowledge of botany, I can appreciate their visual appeal and the positive emotions they evoke. However, I wouldn’t say I’m a passionate flower enthusiast.","My first teacher was a very kind and patient woman named Mrs. Davies. I remember her as having a calming presence and a gentle way of explaining things. She made learning fun through games and creative activities, which was important for a young child. I particularly recall her reading sessions, where she would bring such expressiveness and enthusiasm to the stories that they really came alive. While I don't remember specific lessons, the overall impression I have is one of warmth and encouragement that fostered a positive attitude towards school.","I enjoy reading a variety of books, but I have a particular fondness for historical fiction and biographies. I find historical fiction engaging because it immerses me in different time periods and cultures, allowing me to explore history through the lens of compelling narratives. Occasionally, I'll also read contemporary fiction, depending on the author and subject matter. Ultimately, I'm drawn to books that are well-written, thought-provoking, and offer some form of enriching experience."],"part1_2":["In these pictures, we can see two different travel experiences. The first image shows a girl traveling by train. She seems to be enjoying the scenery as she looks out the window, taking in the beauty of her surroundings. This suggests that train travel can be a more relaxed and scenic way to explore new places. On the other hand, the second picture depicts a family boarding a plane. They are carrying hand luggage and appear to be ready for their flight. This contrast highlights how air travel is often faster and more efficient, especially for long distances. However, it might not offer the same kind of connection to the landscape that train travel does. Overall, both modes of transportation have their unique experiences and benefits.","Travelling by plane can be quite challenging for several reasons. First, there are the long security checks and waiting times at the airport, which can be quite stressful. Passengers often have to arrive several hours before their flight, making the whole process time-consuming. Additionally, flying can be uncomfortable, especially on long-haul flights, as the seating is often cramped and there’s limited legroom. There’s also the issue of flight delays or cancellations, which can disrupt travel plans. Lastly, some people experience anxiety or fear of flying, which can make the journey even more difficult.","Travelling by train has many benefits that make it an appealing option for many people. One of the main advantages is the comfort; trains usually offer more space to move around compared to planes. Passengers can walk around, visit a dining car, or simply enjoy the scenery through large windows. Trains also often have fewer restrictions on luggage, which can make packing easier. Moreover, train stations are usually located in the city center, making it more convenient to reach your final destination. Finally, train travel is often seen as more environmentally friendly than flying, which is an important consideration for many travelers today."],"part2":"There was a time when I had a disagreement with my friend about which movie to watch. We had planned a movie night, and I wanted to see a comedy, but my friend preferred an action film. At first, we were just joking around about it, but then it turned into a bit of a serious discussion. We both felt strongly about our choices, and it was hard to find common ground. Eventually, we decided to compromise by watching one movie first and then the other later. Looking back, it was a bit silly to argue over a movie, but it taught us the importance of communication and being open to each other's preferences. People usually argue with each other when they have different opinions or interests. This can happen in various situations, like during family discussions about plans or decisions, or even among friends when choosing a place to eat. Arguments can also arise in the workplace over projects or responsibilities. Often, misunderstandings or miscommunications lead to disagreements as well. In general, when emotions run high or when people feel strongly about their beliefs, that’s when arguments are most likely to happen. To solve disagreements, I think it’s important to communicate openly and listen to each other’s viewpoints. One suggestion is to stay calm and avoid raising your voice, as this can escalate the situation. It might also help to find common ground or a compromise that satisfies both parties. Another suggestion is to take a break if things get too heated; sometimes stepping away for a moment can help clear your mind. Finally, showing empathy and trying to understand the other person’s feelings can go a long way in resolving conflicts peacefully.","part3":"If those who are under 16 are not allowed to use the internet, this may lead to both some advantages and disadvantages. On the one hand, a ban on internet access for those under 16 would significantly reduce their exposure to harmful online content, including cyberbullying, inappropriate material, and predatory behavior. This would create a safer online environment for young people during a crucial developmental stage where they are particularly vulnerable to manipulation and exploitation. Another plus side is that restricting internet access could encourage a greater focus on traditional learning methods and extracurricular activities. Without the constant distraction of social media and online games, young people might dedicate more time to academic pursuits, physical activity, and social interaction in the real world. Furthermore, a ban would place greater emphasis on parental guidance and family interaction. Parents would play a more direct role in shaping their children's learning experiences and facilitating access to appropriate information. This could foster stronger family bonds and improve communication, providing a better environment for open discussions about appropriate online behavior and the risks of internet usage before responsible access is granted later. However, the negative sides of this approach should be also taken into account. First and foremost, a complete ban on internet access would severely restrict young people's access to a wealth of educational resources available online. This includes online learning platforms, educational videos, research materials, and virtual libraries, all of which can enhance learning and provide opportunities not available through traditional schooling. In addition, the internet plays a crucial role in social interaction for teenagers. Banning access would isolate young people from their peer groups and limit their ability to build and maintain relationships. This could negatively impact their social and emotional development, potentially leading to increased feelings of loneliness, isolation, and difficulty navigating social situations. Finally, the internet is an integral part of modern life. A ban would leave young people unprepared for the demands of a digitally driven world. They would lack the skills and experience necessary to navigate online environments safely and effectively, putting them at a disadvantage in future education, employment, and even everyday life."}},{"id":"mb15","title":"Mock Book · Mock 15","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Do you live in a flat or a house?","What do you usually do to keep fit?","Tell me about your favourite drink."],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","What are the disadvantages of playing on the phone too much?","What are the advantages of playing outside?"],"part1_2_images":["mb15_p12_1.jpg","mb15_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a time when you tried to do something but failed.","When was it and what did you try to do?","Why were you not successful in doing it?"],"part2_image":"mb15_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"All nations need to adopt a single global language.","for":["This would eliminate language barriers","This can lead to better cultural exchange and understanding","No need for translation services and language learning"],"against":["This can lead to the erosion of cultures and local languages","Not all individuals have the same level of access to education","It would take many years for every country's population to master a global language"]},"model":{"part1_1":["I reside in a flat, actually. It's quite cozy and practical for me. I enjoy having easy access to amenities and the convenience of living in a central location. While I appreciate the spaciousness of a house, I think a flat suits my lifestyle better, especially since I enjoy spending time exploring the city and connecting with friends.","Keeping a healthy lifestyle is important to me. I try to have a balanced diet, focusing on fresh fruits, vegetables, and whole grains. I also prioritize regular exercise, aiming for at least 30 minutes of physical activity most days of the week. I find that a combination of cardio and strength training helps to keep me fit and energized.","Actually, my preference in terms of beverages quite diversifies. It depends on what I am having or what I am doing. When I am having lunch, I prefer to drink hot tea rather than fizzy drinks. In contrast, when I am engaged in physical activities, I would like to have mineral water. Or, on chilly days, drinking hot coffee is my cup of tea."],"part1_2":["The images depict contrasting leisure activities. The first shows a boy engrossed in a digital game on his mobile phone, representative of contemporary screen-based entertainment. This contrasts sharply with the second image, which portrays a boy actively engaged in a physical activity—playing basketball outdoors.","Well, excessive phone use definitely has its downsides. For one, it can seriously impact your eyesight, leading to headaches and even long-term vision problems. Beyond that, it can be incredibly addictive, making it hard to focus on other important things like schoolwork or spending quality time with family and friends. You can also end up feeling quite isolated and missing out on real-life experiences","Playing outdoors offers a wealth of benefits. Firstly, it promotes physical activity, which is crucial for maintaining a healthy weight and cardiovascular system. Beyond the physical aspects, being outside exposes you to fresh air and sunlight, which is good for your vitamin D levels and overall mood. Outdoor play often involves social interaction with friends, fostering teamwork, communication skills, and a sense of community. It allows for more creative and imaginative play, unlike structured screen-based games."],"part2":"I remember vividly the time I first took the IELTS exam. I was aiming for a Band 7 overall, which I knew would open up a lot of opportunities for me. I diligently studied for months, focusing on all four skills - listening, reading, writing, and speaking. I even joined a preparation course and practiced with past exam papers. I felt confident going into the test, but unfortunately, I didn't achieve my desired score. I fell short in the writing section, only scoring a Band 6.5. It was a huge disappointment, and I was disheartened. Analyzing my results, I realized that my biggest weakness was structuring my essays and using more complex vocabulary effectively. I had a good grasp of grammar and sentence structure, but my essays lacked a strong flow and didn't demonstrate a sophisticated use of language. The experience was a valuable lesson for me. I realized that simply studying the material wasn't enough. I needed to develop a more strategic approach, focusing on areas where I struggled. I signed up for additional writing lessons, studied specific vocabulary related to academic writing, and practiced writing different essay types under timed conditions. This time, I focused on developing strong arguments, clear paragraphing, and using a wider range of vocabulary to express my ideas. It wasn't an easy process, but I eventually achieved my goal of a Band 7 overall. This experience taught me the importance of identifying your weaknesses, seeking help where necessary, and putting in the hard work to improve.","part3":"The idea of adopting a single global language is a compelling one, offering several potential advantages. It would undoubtedly break down communication barriers, fostering smoother collaboration and understanding between individuals and nations. Imagine the efficiency gained in business negotiations, diplomatic talks, and even everyday travel, without the need for translation services. This could also lead to a more unified global community, promoting cultural exchange and reducing misunderstandings. Furthermore, the vast resources currently spent on language learning and translation could be redirected towards other vital areas. However, this seemingly utopian scenario also presents significant challenges. The adoption of a single language could lead to the erosion of cultural diversity, with minority languages and traditions fading away. The process of learning a new language, particularly for older generations, might be arduous and time-consuming. Furthermore, equitable access to language education would be crucial to ensure that everyone has the opportunity to participate in this new linguistic landscape. The potential for social inequality and exclusion could arise if certain groups lack the resources or access to learn the global language. Ultimately, while a single global language has its merits, the potential consequences for cultural diversity and inclusivity cannot be ignored."}},{"id":"mb16","title":"Mock Book · Mock 16","topics":"","source":"Speaking Mock Book 2025","part1_1":["Have you ever purchased anything online?","Do you prefer to live in the city or countryside?","What do you usually have for breakfast?"],"part1_2":["What do you see in these pictures?","Which is more relaxing: reading a book or watching a movie?","Why do some people prefer reading books?"],"part1_2_images":["mb16_p12_1.jpg","mb16_p12_2.jpg"],"part2":["Describe a situation when you forgave someone or were forgiven by someone.","When should people forgive someone?","What is the impact of forgiveness on relationships?"],"part2_image":"mb16_p2.jpg","part3":{"statement":"All employees should be allowed to work from home permanently.","for":["Enhanced employee well-being and productivity","Significant cost savings for businesses","Access to a broader and more diverse talent pool"],"against":["Difficulties in maintaining team cohesion and collaboration","Challenges in monitoring productivity and ensuring accountability","Blurred work-life boundaries and increased burnout"]},"model":{"part1_1":["No, I have never had such shopping experiences yet. This is because online market is not well developed in our country; you have to wait for ages to receive your order. Therefore I prefer to do shopping in markets simply because you can bargain, touch and feel the product you want to purchase.","I would rather urban life for a number of reasons. First, people can have access to better life standards. For example, students can study in top University branches, and people can get better medical treatment. And there are more entertainment options so that people can spend more quality time with their households, and there opportunities for personal growth.","It depends on how much time I have. If I am not in a rush, I will often have a big breakfast, such as fried eggs with sausages, jam and cereals, and of course hot tea. When I have little time, I have a light breakfast, which includes only a cup of coffee, that’s all."],"part1_2":["Both pictures showcase two various spending time experiences. As for the first one, a girl is sitting under the tree and enjoying reading a book. This shows that she prefers to her spare time for educational purposes. In contrast, the second shows close-knit family members, who are indulging in watching a movie together at home. They are sitting in a cozy room which gives cinematic atmosphere.","For me, watching a movie is far more relaxing than reading a book. Reading often requires a degree of concentration and focus, which can be mentally tiring, especially if the material is complex or demanding. However, watching a movie is a great way to unwind after a long day and switch off completely. The immersive nature of film, with its sights and sounds, makes it a much more effective way for me to de-stress.","I think there are several reasons why some people gravitate towards reading books. Firstly, it offers a far greater degree of immersion and active participation. Unlike a movie, where everything is presented visually, readers must actively construct images and emotions in their minds, fostering deeper engagement with the story. Secondly, books allow for a more personal and intimate connection with the narrative. The pace is entirely under the reader's control, and they can re-read passages, reflect on characters, and fully absorb the details at their own leisure."],"part2":"My younger brother once accidentally damaged my phone – a fairly new and expensive model – by dropping it. My initial reaction was a mix of anger and frustration; it was a careless mistake that resulted in a significant financial loss. However, seeing his genuine distress and remorse, I realised that his actions stemmed from clumsiness rather than malice. Ultimately, I forgave him, partly because I valued our sibling bond more than the monetary value of the phone. The experience, though initially upsetting, reinforced the importance of empathy and understanding in family relationships. Forgiveness is a deeply personal choice, not an obligation. It's most appropriate when the offender shows genuine remorse – not just words, but a demonstrable change in behavior – and the context of the offense is considered. Severe, repeated harm might make forgiveness neither possible nor desirable. Ultimately, the decision rests with the wronged individual; it's about their healing, not condoning the act. Forgiveness plays a very important role in relationships. When someone hurts you, holding onto anger can create distance and tension between people. However, when you choose to forgive, it can help heal those wounds. And Forgiveness can strengthen the bond between people. It shows that you care enough to let go of mistakes and focus on the positive aspects of the relationship. Overall, forgiveness can make relationships healthier and more fulfilling.","part3":"If workers are allowed to continue their work remotely, staying at home, this approach will create both potential benefits and drawbacks. As for plus sides, working from home often leads to improved work-life balance, reducing stress related to commuting and rigid office schedules. This can translate into increased employee morale, higher job satisfaction, and ultimately, greater productivity. Furthermore, reduced commuting costs for employees can indirectly contribute to cost savings. These financial benefits could then be reinvested in other areas of the business, leading to potential growth and improved employee compensation. Finally, removing geographical limitations through a permanent work- from-home policy opens up opportunities to recruit from a much wider talent pool. This allows companies to hire the best candidates, regardless of location, promoting diversity and increasing the chances of finding individuals with unique skills and perspectives. However, potential minus sides should also be taken into account. First, remote work can lead to feelings of isolation among employees, hindering informal communication and spontaneous collaboration that often occurs in a traditional office setting. Another drawback is that supervising remote employees requires different management strategies than those used in a physical office. Accurately measuring individual output and ensuring employees remain accountable for their work can be difficult, requiring a shift in management styles and increased reliance on performance metrics. On top of this, working from home can lead to longer working hours as the boundaries between work and personal life become less defined. Employees may find it difficult to “switch off” at the end of the day, leading to increased stress, burnout, and a negative impact on their overall well-being. This necessitates strong self-discipline and effective time management skills from employees."}}];
